Adapted from: https://github.com/UditAkhourii/adhd
Reviewed commit: 7b91ce601ed951c1a9658c63f6f9550d2486525b
Reviewed date: 2026-10-20
License: MIT; retained in LICENSE
Sources: skills/adhd/SKILL.md, SOURCE-SPEC.md, documentation/how-it-works.md, documentation/frames.md, documentation/evals.md

Adopted: separate generation/evaluation, contrasting cognitive lenses, isolated branch context when authorized, mechanism-based clustering, specific trap reasons, and development into risks and concrete experiments.
Adapted: bounded optional branching, explicit single-session fallback, baseline retained, fit and hard constraints before novelty, uncertainty distinguished from failure, and human steering inherited from the hosting workflow.
Excluded: SDK/CLI installation, fixed branch counts and scoring weights, automatic delegation, bans on obvious solutions, clinical framing, and benchmark superiority claims. Upstream's small engineering evaluation uses model-family judging and does not establish general effectiveness.

Local addition 2026-10-20: optional external seed stimulus inspired by accessible Techniques 1–6 of Anshu Chimala's https://www.lennysnewsletter.com/p/how-to-turn-your-ai-into-a-world . The article ending was paywalled. The shared visual-refinement protocol in cleanui records the related design-workflow adaptations; no article prompt text or model-performance claim is copied.
